cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the repository and the exact release."
title: "MICA machine"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Frank
    family-names: Böhm
version: "0.1.0"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/arcencilo-family/mica-machine"
date-released: "2026-11-16"
abstract: >-
  A pre-release code snapshot of MICA's machine: the readers for its gates, the
  floor that composes their verdicts, the core door that pins the reader code, and
  the evidence tools around them. No probe has yet read READABLE, and a reader that
  cannot assess holds or passes by the declared stakes rather than claiming a pass.
  See the README for the known limits and the tests expected to fail.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - AI safety
  - agents
  - monitoring
  - evidence
